---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import {
  siteConfig,
  homeUrl,
  renderTemplate,
  legalUpdatedLabel,
} from '../lib/site';

const { appName, contactDisplay: contact } = siteConfig;

const sections = [
  { id: 'purpose', label: 'Purpose' },
  { id: 'checking', label: 'How details are checked' },
  { id: 'independence', label: 'Independence' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title={siteConfig.pages.about.title}
  description={renderTemplate(siteConfig.pages.about.description)}
  heading="About this page"
  lede={`A short, independent resource for the ${appName} APK: what it is, what was checked, and how to install it.`}
  updated={legalUpdatedLabel}
  sections={sections}
>
  <h2 id="purpose">Purpose</h2>
  <p>
    This site exists to make one thing easier: getting the {appName} Android app onto a phone,
    tablet or TV without guessing which download button is real. It brings the file details,
    installation steps, device notes and common problems onto a single page.
  </p>
  <p>
    The page is static and small on purpose. There is one direct APK link, placed in the middle of
    the page, and every other download reference scrolls to that section. No account is needed to
    read the page or to reach the file.
  </p>

  <h2 id="checking">How details are checked</h2>
  <p>
    Before a release is listed, the published APK is inspected for its version name, package name,
    minimum Android version, native architectures and file size. Those values are shown on the
    homepage and updated when the developer publishes a new build.
  </p>
  <p>
    The file itself is hosted by the developer outside this site. This site does not re-upload,
    repackage or modify it. If the file at the download link changes, the details on this page may be
    out of date until the next review. Check what your browser shows before installing.
  </p>

  <h2 id="independence">Independence</h2>
  <p>
    This is not an app store listing and is not run by the app’s developer. It is also not
    affiliated with any league, team, broadcaster or streaming service. Names are used only to
    describe the app and the sports it covers.
  </p>
  <p>
    There are no ads or paid placements on this page. The site uses Histats to count visits; that is
    explained in the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Site details are published on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. The address shown there
    is <a href={homeUrl}>{contact}</a>; selecting it returns to the homepage.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
